Elastic flavor placement on pods, behind ElasticJobsViaWorkloadSlicesFlavorChangeFromZero.

A worker group admitted with no pods may move to another flavor when it scales
up. The first admission wrote the first flavor's node labels and tolerations
into the job template, and every later pod is created from that template, so
the moved group ran where the first flavor ran, and a gated pod whose template
label conflicts with the new flavor's could never be fixed: the API server lets
a gated pod only gain nodeSelector keys.

With the gate on, the job reconciler leaves the flavors' node labels and
tolerations out of the template when it starts an elastic job, extending
deferAdmissionCheckNodeSelectorsToPods, and the ElasticJobUngater adds those of
the flavors the active slice assigns to each pod before it removes the gate. A
gated pod that an older template gave a conflicting value is deleted, so its
owner recreates it, unless the slice's own template conflicts too. The gate's
default stays false.

